title Mycelium Braid r3 — the linked-chain verdict reads across a Knot (a chain opened before the cut, settled after)
prompt remember/loop card: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think r1 (crux) and r2 (travels) landed and pushed both remotes. The seated rhythm's third rung is the Knot: a ledger a family runs for years does not carry its whole past unbroken. Mirrored pledge_knot.rye/purse_knot.rye — a BraidKnot pairs the integrity-sealed global supply (cord_knot.seal_dag) with the prefix's account-and-braid map the FoldState omits; continue_braid verifies the Knot, seeds a Ledger with the prefix, and walks the live suffix through the shared braid.fold_link.
think A real honest seam surfaced and shaped the crux: fold's GLOBAL supply law reads a kind_tax fact as a BURN (taxed <= issued), yet the Braid reuses kind_tax as a CONSERVING transfer. A routing chain Alice->Bob->Carol->Dave taxes 100+120+60 = 280 against an issued 150, so seal_dag would refuse Overdraw if the whole chain sat in the prefix. The honest resolution IS the crux: a braid seals only its OPENING (link 0, whose single tax 100 stays within issued 150) and the routing tail rides the live suffix, where the Braid's own conserving law governs rather than fold's global burn. That is exactly what a linked chain across a checkpoint means — begun before the cut, finished after it.
think Because a braid settles only when its final link closes it, the sealed prefix holds the chain OPEN with no coin moved (Alice 100, Bob 50 genesis only, braid pending, 1 link). The suffix carries link1 (Bob->Carol 120) and link2 (Carol->Dave 60, last), in seq order; the final link closes the chain and settle_braid commits the whole atom at once against the seeded prefix balances — Alice 0, Bob 30, Carol 60, Dave 60.
obs GREEN first pass. braids_match proves the full Cord and the Knot-continued verdict never drift (braid/atom counts, issued, every balance, each braid's state and link_count). Conservation (balances_sum == total_issued == 150) holds past the cut. Three integrity refusals hold: a Knot corrupted after sealing (KnotCorrupt, before a link is folded — a runtime verify gate, not an assert), a tampered suffix link (IdentityRefused), a suffix link continuing a chain the checkpoint never opened (BraidBroken — a fresh chain must open at seq 0). TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, braid_knot.rye no findings.
loom witness=mycelium_braid_knot_witness result=GREEN committed_across=1 prefix_pending=1 conserved=150 no_drift=true refusals=3 seal_tax=100_of_issued_150
file mycelium/braid_knot.rye r3 — the linked-chain verdict reads across a Knot; a chain opened in the sealed prefix, settled in the live suffix
